entury, is a crucial chronicle that details the life of Genghis Khan and his immediate successors, particularly Ögedei Khan. Authored around the time of Genghis Khan's death in 1227, this text provides an unparalleled glimpse into the Mongolian Empire during its formative years, covering the social, political, and military structures that supported its expansion. This work is significant not only as a historical document but also as a reflection of Mongolian identity, capturing the ethos and cultural heritage of the Mongols at a pivotal point in their history.

